# Secret-scan exceptions (C-0004, ADR-0017).
#
# This file is the ONLY legitimate way to suppress a secret-scan finding. Inline
# `# gitleaks:allow` comments are disabled everywhere by --ignore-gitleaks-allow in
# templates/infra-ci/scripts/secret-scan.sh, because a comment anyone can append is a
# one-line bypass of the whole control and leaves no reviewable trace.
#
# An entry here is a fingerprint, not a rule. It names one finding in one place:
#
#     <file>:<rule-id>:<line>
#     path/to/file.yaml:paridyum-db-url-with-password:42
#
# Get the fingerprint from the scan output — gitleaks prints `Fingerprint:` for every
# finding. Copy it exactly.
#
# Three things that make this safe where a comment is not:
#
#   1. It appears in a diff, so adding one is a visible act a reviewer sees.
#   2. It is pinned to a line, so it lapses when the file changes and does not silently
#      keep permitting whatever moves into its place.
#   3. It lives in one file, so `wc -l` is an honest count of how much has been waived.
#
# Every entry MUST carry a comment above it stating why the finding is not a real
# secret. An unexplained entry is indistinguishable from a smuggled one, and reviewers
# will wave it through. If you cannot write the reason, it is a real secret — rotate it.
#
# Empty by design. Nothing in this repository needs an exception.
